missing null check before calling `.get()` - will throw `NoSuchElementException` if credential not found

```suggestion
        Optional<CredentialModel> credentialModelOpt = RecoveryAuthnCodesUtils.getCredential(user);
        if (credentialModelOpt.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Recovery codes credential not found for user");
        }
        RecoveryAuthnCodesCredentialModel recoveryCodeCredentialModel = RecoveryAuthnCodesCredentialModel.createFromCredentialModel(credentialModelOpt.get());
```

race condition: the main thread may complete all deletions and set `deletedAll` before the reader thread starts, causing the test to pass without actually testing concurrent access. also, the reader thread isn't joined, so the test may complete before the thread finishes

```suggestion
        AtomicBoolean deletedAll = new AtomicBoolean(false);
        List<Exception> caughtExceptions = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();
        AtomicBoolean readerStarted = new AtomicBoolean(false);

        // read groups in a separate thread
        Thread readerThread = new Thread(() -> {
            readerStarted.set(true);
            while (!deletedAll.get()) {
                try {
                    // just loading briefs
                    managedRealm.admin().groups().groups(null, 0, Integer.MAX_VALUE, true);
                } catch (Exception e) {
                    caughtExceptions.add(e);
                }
            }
        });
        readerThread.start();

        // ensure reader thread starts before deletion
        while (!readerStarted.get()) {
            Thread.sleep(10);
        }

        // delete groups
        groupUuuids.forEach(groupUuid -> {
            managedRealm.admin().groups().group(groupUuid).remove();
        });
        deletedAll.set(true);

        readerThread.join(5000); // wait up to 5 seconds
```
